meta {
  name: file-analysis pre-flight
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/files/analyze/engine
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~provider: ollama
  ~model: qwen2.5:7b
}

docs {
  Whether the provider and model the person picked can run the files tab's model reading: {available:true,provider,model,address} or {available:false,reason,detail,provider?,model?} with reason missing-pair | builtin-model | needs-key. The consent sheet asks this before it offers its send button, so the button never fails after consent (card 604).
  
  Fence: host+origin. Loopback fence plus Origin check: an Origin header, if present, must be loopback. REST clients send no Origin header, which counts as safe — requests pass. A manually added foreign Origin answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
